# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
!.env.example

# vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

.vercel

# local agent/editor configuration
/.agents/
/.claude/settings.local.json

# The pre-write probe is minted per attempt and carries that attempt id as a
# SQL literal. It is transient by construction: committing one would invite
# re-running last week's probe, which is the thing the freshness gate exists to
# refuse. The ATTEMPT LEDGER beside it is the durable record and IS committed.
artifacts/hosted-chain-pre-write-probe.sql
